WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.970
Mind your decisions, I'm Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:04.089 --> 00:00:06.899
Consider a hemisphere whose radius is equal to 10.

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.240
Construct a cube whose bottom face has the same center as the hemisphere.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:18.620
Increase the size of the cube until the four corners of its top face are touching the hemisphere.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:25.020
Now construct a line segment from the center of its top face to a corner of its bottom face.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.220
What is the length of this green line?

00:00:28.680 --> 00:00:31.620
This is adapted from a design exam in India.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:38.320
Pause the video if you'd like to give it a try and when you're ready keep watching to learn how to solve this problem.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:52.940
We'll get started by focusing on just the cube.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:58.880
The green line goes from the center of its top face to a corner of its bottom face.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:07.360
By symmetry, this will be the same distance as going from a corner of its top face to the center of its bottom face.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.180
We'll draw this line in blue.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.980
Now, let's go back to the original diagram and

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:16.690
focus on just the hemisphere.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:23.290
This blue line is exactly a radius of the hemisphere and its radius is equal to 10 meters.

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:31.419
Therefore the length of this line and the green line is 10 meters and it's that simple if you think inside the box.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:37.200
Thanks for making Mind Your Decisions one of the best channels on YouTube.

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:42.620
As always, thanks for watching and thanks for your support.

